nd about 430 to hold, so candidate 4 comes out roughly 450 worse.\n- **Product 1:** the penalty of 8 and margin of 6 justify a buffer. Batches spoil after 4 days, so too much stock is also lost. Ordering 1.1–1.2× looks about right. Candidate 4 (1.1×) may be about 140 ahead of candidate 5 (1.2×). Candidate 7 (1.0×) falls short of expected demand by about 50 units and loses more on penalties.\n- **Candidate 2** orders every day, with about 1.05× for product 0 and 1.15× for product 1. Daily ordering saves about 530 in holding but adds about 670 in fixed order costs. Its product 0 orders are also a little higher. Net, it lands about 200 below candidate 5.\n\n**Under random demand:** candidate 5 has a lean product 0 stock and a buffer in product 1, where shortages cost the most. That makes it the most robust of the group, and capacity stays within limits even when the 163-unit batch arrives on day 22.\n\nExpected-profit order: 5 ≳ 4 ≈ 2 > 7 > 0 > 6, 3 > 1."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3813, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3813}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T00:35:22.458Z", "request_id": "req_011CgPudtf2SeyFNFnMjZsLU"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01Nqnq2ocrDYaBH7bYopVSZv", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgPudtsBAC3paJyeDZktK", "t